      "description": "<div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;color:#222;max-width:760px;\"><h2>Surrealist Clock Artwork on Canvas Panel</h2><p>A distorted clock face mixes Roman and Arabic numerals, with bold white arrows and a splash of sky blue against warm ochre and olive tones. The composition has a playful sense of movement that draws you in for a closer look.</p><h3>Condition</h3><p>Unframed, with a few small surface marks visible in the close-up photos.</p><h3>Details</h3><p>The lower-right signature appears to read &ldquo;Melanie Wolk.&rdquo; An artist by that name exhibited at Artexpo New York in 2010, and <em>Art World News</em> profiled her paintings and prints in 2011. The attribution, medium, and date of this piece are unverified. The reverse has an Aaron Brothers artist's canvas label.</p><h3>Included</h3><p>One unframed 11 &times; 14-inch canvas panel.</p><h3>Packing &amp; Shipping</h3><p>Packed flat in a box with rigid face protection. Buyer-paid calculated shipping. Returns accepted within 30 days, with buyer-paid return shipping.</p></div>",
